tool_notes = Sonnet, Opus, and Haiku all send 9 eager tools (Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, ReportFindings, ScheduleWakeup, Skill, ToolSearch, Write) plus deferred-tool names through ToolSearch in non-interactive (-p) requests; Haiku no longer receives all tool schemas directly the way it did in 2.1.170. AskUserQuestion is excluded from the non-interactive eager set (headless mode cannot prompt the user) but is present in the interactive REPL's 10 eager tools. ReportFindings is new in this version (used to report code-review findings) and is eager in both capture modes. Fable 5 sends the same 9 non-interactive eager tools. Glob and Grep no longer appear in any captured request, eager or ToolSearch-deferred, and prompts now tell models to use `find`/`grep` via Bash instead; tools/Glob.json and tools/Grep.json were removed as stale 2.1.170-era captures. A new deferred-tool name, DesignSync, was observed in the ToolSearch deferred-tools list but its schema was not captured (no ToolSearch selection occurred in this capture round). Tool files with model-specific or capture-mode payload differences contain a variants array.
